cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below. To refer to the bronze artifact itself, use its sigla ET Pa 4.2 (Rix, Etruskische Texte, 1991) or TLE 719."
type: software
title: "The Piacenza Liver: an interactive scholarly visualization"
abstract: >-
  Interactive 3D visualization of the Etruscan bronze Liver of Piacenza
  (late 2nd to early 1st century BCE) presenting all 42 inscriptions with
  transcriptions in Etruscan script, deity mappings, cosmological zones and
  interpretive notes. The 3D model is an artist's reconstruction, not a scan
  of the bronze.
authors:
